ed at least 47 people]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133613838.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A gang in Haiti has freed thirteen hostages, including women and children, following a brutal assault. UNICEF played a crucial role in securing their release from a farming community. This incident in Kenscoff underscores the rampant violence impacting children across Haiti. The region has faced numerous fatalities and displacement due to gang activities, although mass abductions are less frequent and often yield unpredictable results for those abducted.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/haiti-gang-frees-13-women-and-children-days-after-deadly-raid-that-killed-at-least-47-people/articleshow/133613838.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/haiti-gang-frees-13-women-and-children-days-after-deadly-raid-that-killed-at-least-47-people/articleshow/133613838.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-29T20:03:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133614163,imgsize-185752.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[From F1 visa to US citizenship: Indian-origin tech leader says high-skilled Indians have it harder than most but H-1B abuse should 100% stop]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133614103.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/from-f1-visa-to-us-citizenship-indian-origin-tech-leader-says-high-skilled-indians-have-it-harder-than-most-but-h-1b-abuse-should-100-stop/articleshow/133614103.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/from-f1-visa-to-us-citizenshi