ia.indiatimes.com/world/us/as-lindsay-clancy-jury-deliberates-us-mother-found-not-guilty-in-deaths-of-2-children/articleshow/133613084.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-29T19:20:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133613314,imgsize-69906.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[324-million-year-old insect still had swimming paddles]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133611289.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A remarkable fossil unearthed in Texas sheds light on the evolutionary journey of insects transitioning from aquatic to terrestrial life. This ancient species featured paddle-like limbs designed for swimming and additional legs on its abdomen, indicating a semi-aquatic lifestyle in shallow coastal regions. This find is crucial in understanding the slow, gradual adaptations insects underwent over millions of years in their evolutionary history.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/a-324-million-year-old-fossil-from-texas-preserves-an-early-insect-with-24-legs-and-paddle-like-limbs-on-its-abdomen-suggesting-insects-did-not-leave-water-for-land-in-one-sudden-evolutionary-jump/articleshow/133611289.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/a-324-million-year-old-fossil-from-texas-preserves-an-early-insect-with-24-legs-and-paddle-like-limbs-on-its-abdomen-suggesting-insects-did-not-leave-water-for-land-in-one-sudden-evolutionary-jump/articleshow/133611289.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-29T17:31:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133611339,imgsize-112092.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ex-White House teleprompter operator fined $65,000 for betting on Trump speeches]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133611588.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ex-white-house-teleprompter-operator-fined-65000-for-betting-on-trump-speeches/articleshow/133611588.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ex-white-house-teleprompter-operator-fined-65000-for-betting-on-trump-speeches/articleshow/133611588.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-29T17:46:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133611735,imgsize-71275.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Hurricane Katrina forced New Orleans’ Charity Hospital to close in 2005; now it is being transformed into a $500 million medical research hub]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133607914.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The historic Charity Hospital in New Orleans is set to undergo a remarkable transformation into a cutting-edge medical research facility. Spearheaded by Tulane University, this ambitious $500 million project aims to establish a vibrant biomedical innovation hub, with construction kicking off this fall and projected completion by 2029. This redevelopment not only honors the landmark's legacy but also demonstrates a robust commitment to improving healthcare for the Gulf South community.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/hurricane-katrina-forced-new-orleans-charity-hospital-to-close-in-2005-21-years-later-the-million-sq-ft-building-is-being-transformed-into-a-500-million-medical-research-hub/articleshow/133607914.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/hurricane-katrina-forced-new-orleans-charity-hospital-to-close-in-2005-21-years-later-the-million-sq-ft-building-is-being-transformed-into-a-500-million-medical-research-hub/articleshow/133607914.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-29T17:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133607968,imgsize-95464.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Virginia farmer helps create 2,500-acre wildlife corridor through conservation]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133609901.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Two innovative farmers in Virginia are taking strides to connect wildlife habitats on their private lands. Their commitment to blending agriculture with biodiversity creates crucial corridors for wildlife, allowing seamless movement between expansive protected areas. Backed by various scientific and conservation programs, their initiative protects about 2,500 acres of important terrain, fostering a sustainable environment for diverse species.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-virginia-farmer-protected-his-land-from-development-and-persuaded-his-neighbours-to-follow-25-years-later-nearly-2500-acres-of-private-farms-now-form-a-wildlife-corridor/articleshow/133609901.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-virginia-farmer-protected-his-land-from-development-and-persuaded-his-neighbours-to-follow-25-years-later-nearly-2500-acres-of-private-farms-now-form-a-wildlife-corridor/articleshow/133609901.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-29T17:48:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133609923,imgsize-51086.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[43-acre Virginia farm behind an inclusive riding programme for people with disabilities listed for $8.4 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133609964.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Wheatland Equestrian's historic Virginia property is being sold for approximately $8.4 million.  This sale will support the Faith and Family Foundation's long-term mission.  The organization began in 1999, offering inclusive equestrian opportunities for all riders.  It gained national recognition as a USEF Para-Dressage Center of Excellence.  The proceeds will ensure continued services for children and adults with disabilities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1999-a-virginia-couple-founded-a-nonprofit-riding-programme-for-people-with-disabilities-after-it-became-a-usef-center-of-excellence-their-historic-43-acre-farm-is-listed-for-8-4-million-to-fund-future-services/articleshow/133609964.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1999-a-virginia-couple-founded-a-nonprofit-riding-programme-for-people-with-disabilities-after-it-became-a-usef-center-of-excellence-their-historic-43-acre-farm-is-listed-for-8-4-million-to-fund-future-services/articleshow/133609964.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-29T16:22:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133610019,imgsize-1141780.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Minnesota removed common carp; lake clarity rose nearly 600% afterward]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133609602.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Pickerel Lake, Minnesota, has battled significant water quality and algal bloom problems for decades, primarily due to invasive common carp taking over the shallow waters. After their removal in 2009, the lake underwent a remarkable ecological revival, with water clarity significantly improving and native aquatic plants flourishing once more. This successful restoration highlights the pivotal role of addressing invasive species in revitalizing ecosystems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2009-minnesota-treated-pickerel-lake-with-fish-poison-to-remove-common-carp-afterward-water-clarity-rose-nearly-600-and-plant-cover-climbed-from-4-6-to-90/articleshow/133609602.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2009-minnesota-treated-pickerel-lake-with-fish-poison-to-remove-common-carp-afterward-water-clarity-rose-nearly-600-and-plant-cover-climbed-from-4-6-to-90/articleshow/133609602.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-29T15:56:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133609652,imgsize-169955.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Burnham differs from Starmer on assisted dying bill, will skip vote to avoid influencing debate]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133609984.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/andy-burnham-differs-from-starmer-on-assisted-dying-bill-will-skip-vote-to-avoid-influencing-debate/articleshow/133609984.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/andy-burnham-differs-from-starmer-on-assisted-dying-bill-will-skip-vote-to-avoid-influencing-debate/articleshow/133609984.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-29T16:33:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aashish Vashistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133610310,imgsize-89485.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Viking woman’s clothes preserved by her jewellery for 1,300 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133608734.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Danish archaeologists discovered rare Viking textile remains near Varde.  Corrosion from jewelry preserved these ancient wool and linen fragments.  This discovery offers a rare glimpse into Viking dress from 1,300 years ago.  Researchers will analyze the fibers and teeth for more information.  Dating the textiles will reveal if ornaments were new or inherited.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/rare-textile-fragments-have-survived-for-around-1300-years-inside-a-viking-womans-danish-grave-because-metallic-salts-released-by-two-brooches-inhibited-microbes-that-would-normally-destroy-the-cloth/articleshow/133608734.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/rare-textile-fragments-have-survived-for-around-1300-years-inside-a-viking-womans-danish-grave-because-metallic-salts-released-by-two-brooches-inhibited-microbes-that-would-normally-destroy-the-cloth/articleshow/133608734.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-29T15:11:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133608859,imgsize-423678.cms"/></item></channel></rss>